    "rationale": "The dilution linearity tests provide strong evidence that the OD600 plate reader responded proportionally throughout the plateau phase (h6-18). At hour 18, the 2x dilution (0.2161) is approximately half the undiluted reading (0.4469), confirming linear response with no detector saturation. At hour 12, similar proportionality was observed (0.2283 ≈ 0.4266/2). These results indicate the plate reader was accurately measuring biomass concentration and was not saturated. The plateau in OD readings from h6-18 (mean ~0.42) reflects an actual plateau in biomass concentration, consistent with cells entering and remaining in stationary phase. There is no evidence of cryptic biomass accumulation, aggregation-induced optical artifacts, or reader saturation that would indicate biomass higher than the readings suggest. The culture's biomass at h18 is at the level the undiluted reading (≈0.42 OD600) indicates."
